    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0352" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg312"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 926.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 13, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Under the directions contained in your No.
                    1278, of the 25th of February, I addressed a note to Lord Russell on the 15th of
                    March, on the subject of the visit to Nassau of the United States steamer
                    Honduras, a copy of which <pb facs="0353" n="313" xml:id="pg313"/> is herewith
                    transmitted. His lordship has replied to the separate points in two notes of the
                    same date, the 5th of April, copies of which are also sent.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d172-a1.xml" xpointer="d172-a1"/>
            </div>
